      <section>
        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

        <div class="not-prose space-y-6 my-6">

          <div class="border border-border rounded-lg p-5">
            <p class="font-semibold text-heading mb-2">What is the Cornell Ergonomics seat depth rule?</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Cornell Ergonomics research defines correct seat depth as leaving 2&#8211;3 finger-widths (approximately 2&#8211;3 inches) of clearance between the front edge of the seat cushion and the back of your knees when sitting fully against the backrest. This clearance prevents the seat edge from pressing into the popliteal region &#8212; the soft tissue behind the knee &#8212; which can restrict blood flow and compress the tibial nerve. For tall users, meeting this rule typically requires a minimum seat depth of 18&#8211;20 inches, well above the 15&#8211;17 inches found on most standard office chairs.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="border border-border rounded-lg p-5">
            <p class="font-semibold text-heading mb-2">How much seat depth do I need if I'm 6'3"?</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">At 6&#39;3&#34;, most users fall in the 6&#39;2&#34;&#8211;6&#39;4&#34; range that typically requires 19&#8211;20 inches of seat depth. The exact number depends on your thigh length (hip to back of knee), not height alone. To measure: sit against a flat wall on a firm surface with feet flat, then measure from the wall to a point 2&#8211;3 inches in front of your knee crease. That is your minimum required seat depth. Users with longer-than-average legs relative to their height will need more; those with shorter legs relative to height may need slightly less.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="border border-border rounded-lg p-5">
            <p class="font-semibold text-heading mb-2">Can a seat that's too shallow cause knee pain?</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Yes. When a seat is too shallow for a user&#39;s thigh length, the front edge of the seat cushion presses directly into the popliteal region &#8212; the soft tissue behind the knee where the popliteal artery, tibial nerve, and major tendons pass close to the surface. Sustained pressure here restricts blood flow to the lower leg, compresses the tibial nerve, and creates the characteristic pain, tingling, and numbness that builds throughout the workday. The longer the session, the more pronounced the discomfort becomes as circulation restriction compounds.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="border border-border rounded-lg p-5">
            <p class="font-semibold text-heading mb-2">What's the difference between fixed and adjustable seat depth?</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">A fixed seat depth chair has one seat pan measurement with no adjustment &#8212; if it does not match your thigh length, there is no mechanical fix. An adjustable seat depth chair uses a seat slider mechanism that extends the seat pan forward independently of the backrest, typically offering 2&#8211;4 inches of range. For tall users, adjustable seat depth is strongly preferable because it lets you dial in the exact 2&#8211;3 inch clearance at the knee regardless of your precise thigh length. The Steelcase Leap Plus and Steelcase Gesture both use seat sliders; the Herman Miller Aeron Size C has a fixed depth.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="border border-border rounded-lg p-5">
            <p class="font-semibold text-heading mb-2">Does the Herman Miller Aeron have enough seat depth for tall users?</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">The Herman Miller Aeron Size C has a fixed seat depth of approximately 18.5 inches. This is workable for users in the 6&#39;0&#34;&#8211;6&#39;2&#34; range with average thigh proportions. However, users 6&#39;3&#34; and taller, or users with longer-than-average femurs relative to their height, may find this depth marginal or insufficient &#8212; particularly if their measured minimum requirement is 19 inches or more. The Aeron&#39;s fixed depth means there is no slider to extend it further, so users above this threshold should consider the Steelcase Leap Plus, which reaches 19.75 inches of adjustable seat depth.</p>
          </div>

        </div>
      </section>

    </div>

      <nav class="mt-8 pt-6 border-t border-border" aria-label="Related accessory guides">
        <p class="text-sm font-medium text-muted-foreground mb-3">Related fit guides:</p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
          <li><a href="/seat-cushion-height-tall-people/" class="link-internal text-muted-foreground">Seat cushion to increase chair height →</a></li>
          <li><a href="/lumbar-support-tall-people/" class="link-internal text-muted-foreground">Lumbar support for tall people and long torsos →</a></li>
        </ul>
      </nav>

      <nav class="mt-8 pt-6 border-t border-border" aria-label="Related chair guides">
        <p class="text-sm font-medium text-muted-foreground mb-3">Other chair guides:</p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
          <li><a href="/wide-seat-office-chairs-tall-people/" class="link-internal text-muted-foreground">Wide seat office chairs for tall and broad frames →</a></li>
          <li><a href="/heavy-duty-ergonomic-chairs-tall-people/" class="link-internal text-muted-foreground">Heavy-duty ergonomic chairs (weight capacity + tall fit) →</a></li>
        </ul>
      </nav>
  </article>
</Layout>

<script>
  const depthByHeight: Record<string, Record<string, number>> = {
    '6.0': { short: 17.5, average: 18.0, long: 18.5 },
    '6.1': { short: 18.0, average: 18.5, long: 19.0 },
    '6.2': { short: 18.5, average: 19.0, long: 19.5 },
    '6.3': { short: 19.0, average: 19.5, long: 20.0 },
    '6.4': { short: 19.5, average: 20.0, long: 20.5 },
    '6.5': { short: 20.0, average: 20.5, long: 21.0 },
  };

  const chairs = [
    {
      name: 'Steelcase Leap Plus',
      depth: '15.75–19.75″ (adjustable)',
      maxDepth: 19.75,
      url: '/review/leap-plus/',
      amazon: 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B00TYE4QXU?tag=tallchairadvi-20',
    },
    {
      name: 'Steelcase Gesture',
      depth: '15.75–18.75″ (adjustable)',
      maxDepth: 18.75,
      url: '/review/gesture/',
      amazon: 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B016OIF2JU?tag=tallchairadvi-20',
    },
    {
      name: 'Herman Miller Aeron Size C',
      depth: '~18.5″ (fixed)',
      maxDepth: 18.5,
      url: '/review/aeron-size-c/',
      amazon: 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B01N32UFNT?tag=tallchairadvi-20',
    },
  ];

  let selectedHeight: string | null = null;

  const step1 = document.getElementById('calc-step1')!;
  const step2 = document.getElementById('calc-step2')!;
  const resultsEl = document.getElementById('calc-results')!;
  const resultDepthEl = document.getElementById('result-depth')!;
  const resultNoteEl = document.getElementById('result-note')!;
  const resultChairsEl = document.getElementById('result-chairs')!;
  const manualToggle = document.getElementById('manual-toggle')!;
  const manualSection = document.getElementById('calc-manual')!;
  const inseamInput = document.getElementById('inseam-input') as HTMLInputElement;
  const manualCalcBtn = document.getElementById('manual-calc-btn')!;

  function showResults(minDepth: number, note: string) {
    resultDepthEl.textContent = minDepth.toFixed(1);
    resultNoteEl.textContent = note;

    const matching = chairs.filter((c) => c.maxDepth >= minDepth);
    const notMatching = chairs.filter((c) => c.maxDepth < minDepth);

    let html = '';
    matching.forEach((c) => {
      html += `<div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 p-3 rounded-lg border border-green-200 bg-green-50">
        <div>
          <span class="text-xs font-semibold text-green-700 uppercase tracking-wide">Covers your requirement</span>
          <p class="font-medium text-heading text-sm mt-0.5"><a href="${c.url}" class="link-internal">${c.name}</a></p>
          <p class="text-xs text-muted-foreground">${c.depth}</p>
        </div>
        <a href="${c.amazon}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer sponsored" data-affiliate-cta="true" data-affiliate-program="amazon" data-affiliate-class="chair" data-cta-label="View ${c.name} on Amazon" data-cta-position="calculator-result" class="shrink-0 text-xs bg-primary text-primary-foreground px-3 py-1.5 rounded-md font-medium hover:bg-primary/90 transition-colors">View on Amazon &rarr;</a>
      </div>`;
    });
    notMatching.forEach((c) => {
      html += `<div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 p-3 rounded-lg border border-border bg-secondary/20 opacity-60">
        <div>
          <span class="text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wide">May be marginal</span>
          <p class="font-medium text-heading text-sm mt-0.5"><a href="${c.url}" class="link-internal">${c.name}</a></p>
          <p class="text-xs text-muted-foreground">${c.depth}</p>
        </div>
      </div>`;
    });

    resultChairsEl.innerHTML = html;
    resultsEl.classList.remove('hidden');
  }

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.height-btn').forEach((btn) => {
    btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      document.querySelectorAll('.height-btn').forEach((b) => {
        b.classList.remove('border-primary', 'text-primary', 'bg-primary/5');
      });
      btn.classList.add('border-primary', 'text-primary', 'bg-primary/5');
      selectedHeight = btn.dataset.height!;
      step2.classList.remove('hidden');
      resultsEl.classList.add('hidden');
      document.querySelectorAll('.body-btn').forEach((b) => {
        b.classList.remove('border-primary', 'bg-primary/5');
      });
    });
  });

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.body-btn').forEach((btn) => {
    btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      if (!selectedHeight) return;
      document.querySelectorAll('.body-btn').forEach((b) => {
        b.classList.remove('border-primary', 'bg-primary/5');
      });
      btn.classList.add('border-primary', 'bg-primary/5');

      const bodyType = btn.dataset.body as 'short' | 'average' | 'long';
      const minDepth = depthByHeight[selectedHeight][bodyType];
      const notes: Record<string, string> = {
        short: 'Based on shorter-than-average legs relative to your height.',
        average: 'Based on average leg-to-torso proportions.',
        long: 'Based on longer-than-average legs relative to your height — measure your inseam to confirm.',
      };
      showResults(minDepth, notes[bodyType]);
    });
  });

  manualToggle.addEventListener('click', () => {
    manualSection.classList.toggle('hidden');
  });

  manualCalcBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    const inseam = parseFloat(inseamInput.value);
    if (isNaN(inseam) || inseam < 26 || inseam > 42) {
      inseamInput.classList.add('border-red-400');
      return;
    }
    inseamInput.classList.remove('border-red-400');
    const minDepth = Math.round(inseam * 0.56 * 2) / 2;
    showResults(minDepth, `Based on a ${inseam}" standing inseam measurement.`);
    if (!step2.classList.contains('hidden') === false) {
      step2.classList.remove('hidden');
    }
  });
</script>